+/* citation lines are ~95% of a frame's raster cost (every other part together is a few ms), so they are drawn
+   in screen space with each segment clipped to the visible rectangle (long off-screen tails used to be rasterised
+   too) and, on the main map, kept in an offscreen bitmap (EC) that is blitted while the view is zooming or panning
+   or only the hover changes, and rebuilt exactly when the view settles. edgeEpoch counts every change to node
+   positions or visibility, so the bitmap is never stale; while the simulation runs it is not used. */
